1
00:00:01,870 --> 00:00:28,510
A Real Stewart

2
00:00:28,510 --> 00:00:29,970
It's almost ten o'clock.

3
00:00:29,970 --> 00:00:33,490
I've got to go. Tomorrow is Monday,

4
00:00:33,490 --> 00:00:35,970
and work begins at eight in the morning for me.

5
00:00:35,970 --> 00:00:37,990
Oh, I'm so happy that Max is home.

6
00:00:37,990 --> 00:00:40,620
He's the sweetest little thing.

7
00:00:40,620 --> 00:00:42,580
I'll drive you to the station, dear.

8
00:00:42,580 --> 00:00:46,590
You can catch the ten-twenty train to Grand Central Station.

9
00:00:46,590 --> 00:00:48,780
I'll drive Susan, dear.

10
00:00:48,780 --> 00:00:50,210
Thank you, Philip.

11
00:00:50,210 --> 00:00:51,580
Then Grandpa, Robbie,

12
00:00:51,580 --> 00:01:12,300
and I can finish wrapping all these gifts.

13
00:01:12,300 --> 00:01:16,300
It's so good to have you home again ...

14
00:01:16,300 --> 00:01:22,850
and to see Max asleep in his bassinet at home with us.

15
00:01:22,850 --> 00:01:29,390
To be with our family and all that Stewart TLC.

16
00:01:29,390 --> 00:01:36,340
TLC--tender loving care.

17
00:01:36,340 --> 00:01:39,960
That's our motto.

18
00:01:39,960 --> 00:01:41,060
Did you see the washcloth

19
00:01:41,060 --> 00:01:44,350
and the towels with the teddy bears on them?

20
00:01:44,350 --> 00:01:47,910
Alexandra and the Molinas sent them for Max.

21
00:01:47,910 --> 00:01:50,660
It was so kind of them.

22
00:01:50,660 --> 00:01:52,950
Now Max has come into everyone's life.

23
00:01:52,950 --> 00:01:56,580
The house is so alive with him here.

24
00:01:56,580 --> 00:02:00,040
The welcome sign over the door.

25
00:02:00,040 --> 00:02:02,640
The boxes of presents.

26
00:02:02,640 --> 00:02:05,110
The M-A-X over his bassinet.

27
00:02:05,110 --> 00:02:07,980
Robbie put that there.

28
00:02:07,980 --> 00:02:09,850
Susan's teddy bear.

29
00:02:09,850 --> 00:02:17,520
So cuddly. The beautiful crib from Mom and Dad.

30
00:02:17,520 --> 00:02:22,160
Oh, and Grandpa's baseball glove.

31
00:02:22,160 --> 00:02:24,850
You know, it hung over my crib, too.

32
00:02:24,850 --> 00:02:27,510
And it hung over Robbie's crib.

33
00:02:27,510 --> 00:02:29,210
Part of Grandpa's magic?

34
00:02:29,210 --> 00:02:31,080
Oh, that's not all.

35
00:02:31,080 --> 00:02:32,820
It hung over Susan's crib.

36
00:02:32,820 --> 00:02:34,260
The same baseball glove?

37
00:02:34,260 --> 00:02:39,060
That's right. Grandpa hangs it there for good luck.

38
00:02:39,060 --> 00:02:43,940
He says it always brought him good luck on the baseball team.

39
00:02:43,940 --> 00:02:48,050
He believes it'll bring good luck to all the Stewart babies.

40
00:02:48,050 --> 00:02:49,380
And then he takes it back

41
00:02:49,380 --> 00:02:50,160
when Max is ready to use it?

42
00:02:50,160 --> 00:02:51,200
Yes,

43
00:02:51,200 --> 00:02:53,140
and replaces it with a new glove

44
00:02:53,140 --> 00:02:55,210
so the old one will be ready

45
00:02:55,210 --> 00:02:58,800
for a new member of the Stewart family.

46
00:02:58,800 --> 00:03:04,350
Grandpa really loves his family, doesn't he?

47
00:03:04,350 --> 00:03:07,120
So do I.

48
00:03:07,120 --> 00:03:14,660
And so do I.

49
00:03:14,660 --> 00:03:16,840
And so does Max.

50
00:03:16,840 --> 00:03:19,840
After he eats!
